From 454b0c9c6817a71d749c3ed3ee173a46df9085cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bare <git@barebrowser.org>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 23:03:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Keep the bottom bar on the new tab page

Opening a new tab left the browser with no bottom bar: the buttons were not
hidden, they were never created, and the address bar jumped back to the top.
Every other page kept the bar.

disable_on_ntp is a cached parameter of AndroidBottomBar and its upstream
default is true. Bare never saw that, because the field trial testing config
sets it to false: study GlicAndroid, arm
Enabled_Arm2_BottomBar_1A_with_GLIC_filled, which also enables the feature.
Every earlier build compiled that config in. Setting
disable_fieldtrial_testing_config for the release build returned the parameter
to its upstream default and took the bar off the new tab page. The feature
itself is enabled by default, which is why the bar survived everywhere else.

The default is false here, so the behaviour is the same whatever the field trial
does. Patch 0028 already sets show_bottom_bar_on_gts in the same block for the
same reason.

Two consumers read it, BottomBarConfigUtils.shouldDisableOnNtp and
ToolbarVariationUtils.shouldModifyToolbarButtons, the second being why the
toolbar layout moved as well.

The parameter is read through BooleanCachedFeatureParam, which returns a value
cached in shared preferences and refreshed for the next launch, so the change
lands one launch after the build that carries it.

This is the fourth thing disable_fieldtrial_testing_config uncovered, after the
navigation blur it was added for, the identity disc in 0116 and the password
manager row in 0117. The earlier sweep missed it because it compared
which features the config turns on and off and never compared their parameters.
---
 .../org/chromium/chrome/browser/flags/ChromeFeatureList.java    | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/flags/android/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/flags/ChromeFeatureList.java b/chrome/browser/flags/android/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/flags/ChromeFeatureList.java
index 473981ed9c0..5480d30e3ba 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/flags/android/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/flags/ChromeFeatureList.java
+++ b/chrome/browser/flags/android/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/flags/ChromeFeatureList.java
@@ -2025,7 +2025,7 @@ public abstract class ChromeFeatureList {
     public static final BooleanCachedFeatureParam sAndroidBottomBarBypassGlicGeofencing =
             newBooleanCachedFeatureParam(ANDROID_BOTTOM_BAR, "bypass_glic_geofencing", false);
     public static final BooleanCachedFeatureParam sAndroidBottomBarDisableOnNtp =
-            newBooleanCachedFeatureParam(ANDROID_BOTTOM_BAR, "disable_on_ntp", true);
+            newBooleanCachedFeatureParam(ANDROID_BOTTOM_BAR, "disable_on_ntp", false);
     public static final BooleanCachedFeatureParam sAndroidBottomBarKeepAppMenuInToolbar =
             newBooleanCachedFeatureParam(ANDROID_BOTTOM_BAR, "keep_app_menu_in_toolbar", false);
     public static final BooleanCachedFeatureParam sAndroidBottomBarKeepHomeButtonInToolbar =
